            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\nHmmm... I am not sure what to tell you here, as it doesn't look like 'mini.indentscope' issue, but rather how you install it. I can not reproduce this if installed using built-in packages (manually clone into some `pack/*/opt` and execute `:packadd`).\r\n\r\nHere are first steps i'd take to debug this:\r\n- What does executing `:lua print(MiniIndentscope)` show? It should show something like `table: 0x...`. If not (like `nil`), probably `setup()` function is somehow not called.\r\n- What does executing `:au MiniIndentscope` show? It should show several autocommands calling `MiniIndentscope.auto_draw()`. If not, again `setup()` was not called properly or autocommands got deleted.",
